From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strix Halo Packaging <packaging@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backport: Pixtral axial RoPE compatibility for Transformers 5.17+

Upstream: vllm-project/vllm#56108, "[CI] Bump Transformers version to
5.17.0", merge commit ec4a3a537068db40afbc9374a67da719c8c9b964 (main,
2026-09-16, first released in v0.31.0).

Transformers 5.17 renamed PixtralRotaryEmbedding to
PixtralVisionRotaryEmbedding, switched it to axial RoPE over 2D (height,
width) positions, and removed position_ids_in_meshgrid. On v0.30.0 that makes
`import vllm.model_executor.models.pixtral` raise ImportError, and with it the
ten modules that import it: bee, granite4_vision, lightonocr, llava,
llava_next, llava_next_video, llava_onevision, mistral3, phi4siglip and rvl.

Carried: the vllm/model_executor/models/pixtral.py hunks, unchanged. They
keep the pre-5.17 names working behind a Transformers version check.

Not carried from the same commit: vllm/model_executor/models/laguna.py,
vllm/transformers_utils/config.py (the Laguna config handling and the
process-wide validate_rope change), vllm/transformers_utils/configs/
(__init__.py, laguna.py, mellum.py), vllm/models/qwen4_exp/ and
requirements/test/. Laguna stays unsupported on Transformers 5.18.

Drop at the first packaged vLLM release that contains ec4a3a53.

